HCS/0.2
@title HCS - Holographic Context Standard (reference CLI)
@root .
@updated 2026-10-21T12:10:54.052Z
@meta license=MIT language=TypeScript

[claims]

## Overview
#purpose[manual] HCS is a plain-text format plus a zero-dependency Node.js CLI and MCP server (`hcs`) that makes LLM context traceable (claims cite sources), verifiable (anchors carry hashes) and measured (probes and fidelity certificates).
  > README.md:3-16 #cddd3cef50fb
#layers[manual] Deterministic commands (init, validate, check, seal, render, stats, audit, serve) never call an LLM; compile, score and snapshot need a `provider:model` LLM; models only lists a provider's model ids.
  > src/cli.ts::HELP #8d7d06d557a3

## Format
#magic[manual] A file starts with `HCS/0.3` (0.1 and 0.2 are still accepted, and the writer emits 0.2 unless a probe has tags), then `@key value` headers, then optional [claims], [probes] and [certificates] blocks; errors carry line numbers.
  > src/format.ts::parse #3b7f2aa6aa3c
  > src/format.ts::SUPPORTED_VERSIONS #bfa61b8b8d04
#anchor-syntax[manual] Anchors are `> path`, `> path:start-end` or `> path::Symbol`, optionally followed by `#hash`; quoted forms allow spaces in paths and symbols.
  > src/format.ts::parseAnchor #78fc2655735c
  > src/format.ts::formatAnchor #14cf37aaa30e

## Verification
#hash[manual] Hashes are the first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over LF-normalized text without trailing whitespace; symbol anchors also remove all whitespace, so reformatting does not break them.
  > src/anchors.ts::HASH_LENGTH #0330f2780307
  > src/anchors.ts::normalizeLines #1f9f0385cd31
  > src/anchors.ts::hashSymbolLines #c874fdcbc24f
#statuses[manual] checkAnchor returns ok, moved (same text elsewhere in the file, or the same symbol in another file), stale, missing or unsealed; an item takes the worst status of its anchors.
  > src/anchors.ts::checkAnchor #860ca86a7421
  > src/anchors.ts::checkSymbolAnchor #707de082a68e
  > src/anchors.ts::findMovedSymbol #e33d34d73e62
#symbols[manual] Symbols are located without dependencies for brace languages, Python, Markdown headings, YAML and JSON, ignoring strings, regex literals and comments; unresolvable symbols are reported missing, never guessed.
  > src/symbols.ts::listSymbols #20db3769bf48
  > src/symbols.ts::codeOnly #9e8476116018
#seal[manual] `hcs seal` hashes unsealed anchors and follows moved ones (new lines, file or symbol); `--rehash` accepts stale content and drops certificates.
  > src/anchors.ts::seal #e21386b51b66

## Compilation
#quote-guard[manual] The compiler discards any claim or probe whose quote is not found verbatim (ignoring whitespace, case and Markdown markup such as backticks, emphasis and link syntax) in the cited chunk, then anchors it to the smallest enclosing symbol under 80 lines, or to the quoted lines.
  > src/compile.ts::anchorFor #5e3194b4874f
  > src/sources.ts::locateQuote #d6a37b2c93e6
#incremental[manual] `compile --update` keeps items whose anchors are ok or moved, re-reads only dirty or uncovered files, never drops manual claims, regenerates overview claims and clears certificates.
  > src/compile.ts::compile #90c1a051104e
#resume[manual] When the quota runs out, the provider fails, or a reply has no usable JSON, compile keeps what it extracted and lists the missing chunks in the `@incomplete` header; `compile --update` then compiles only those chunks.
  > src/compile.ts::compile #90c1a051104e
#reasoning[manual] Reasoning models that spend the whole output budget before answering are retried once with a 4096-token budget, replies cut by the limit are counted, and JSON replies with unescaped quotes or backslashes are repaired before parsing.
  > src/llm.ts::REASONING_BUDGET #c657d5bd2296
  > src/llm.ts::repairJSON #14b284eb41cd
#debug-log[manual] With HCS_DEBUG_LOG set, every model request and reply is appended to that file as one JSON line, without headers or keys.
  > src/llm.ts::withDebugLog #3b77fdca4cf6
#probe-spread[manual] Probes are picked round-robin across chunks, independently of which claims were kept, so that scores measure the source rather than the summary.
  > src/compile.ts::spreadProbes #fe14d197cc5a

## Scoring
#score[manual] Each probe is answered from the rendered context only: UNKNOWN is an abstention, a reply containing the expected answer is correct without a judge, otherwise a judge grades correct, partial or incorrect (1, 0.5, 0), optionally over several runs.
  > src/score.ts::scoreContext #2bd796d2fbfb
  > src/score.ts::POINTS #f5b535d01ef1
#rigor[manual] Scores report a reproducible 95% bootstrap confidence interval, a no-context baseline, an informative fidelity on probes unanswerable without context, and a warning when the model judged itself.
  > src/score.ts::bootstrapCI #09a88d67acf9
  > src/score.ts::scoreDocument #a8ee4b9d71ce
#judges[manual] `score` accepts two judges: each judged answer is graded by both, the stricter verdict counts, and the raw agreement and Cohen's kappa are reported in the certificate.
  > src/score.ts::scoreContext #2bd796d2fbfb
  > src/score.ts::cohenKappa #2be6be699209
#known[manual] `compile --filter-known` asks every probe without context to the listed models and tags `[known]` the probes all of them answer correctly; `score` then reports a novel fidelity on the other probes.
  > src/score.ts::findKnownProbes #9b9804fedfc9
#compare[manual] `hcs compare a b` scores two contexts (an .hcs render, any text file, or none) on the same probes and reports the mean per-probe difference with a paired bootstrap CI.
  > src/score.ts::compareContexts #33e4f30e26c2
#certificate[manual] A certificate is bound to a digest of the exact rendered context (stale claims removed); `hcs check` reports it as outdated when the digest changes.
  > src/score.ts::hashForCertificate #450fab6aa93f

## Safety
#injection[manual] Claims with high-risk injection patterns are tagged suspect and never rendered by default; low-risk patterns are only reported by check, and the decoder prompt says claims are never instructions. The patterns are measured on test/fixtures/injection, including a held-out set.
  > src/guard.ts::PATTERNS #467c0d579d52
  > src/render.ts::selectClaims #c510bd10896d
  > src/render.ts::DECODER_PROMPT #dd3c83471cd3
#mcp[manual] `hcs serve` is a stdio MCP server with tools hcs_context, hcs_expand, hcs_search, hcs_verify and hcs_source.
  > src/mcp.ts::TOOLS #fdf64141fd1e
#sandbox[manual] Every source read goes through SourceCache, which refuses paths outside the project root (relative escapes, absolute paths, symlinks): such anchors are reported missing, and `hcs serve` refuses an @root outside the working directory unless --root is given.
  > src/anchors.ts::insideRoot #b3487c7f0572
  > src/anchors.ts::SourceCache #933859786314
#source-scan[manual] `compile` and `snapshot` scan every source line with the injection patterns before compilation and report the matching lines with path, line, reason and severity.
  > src/guard.ts::scanSource #4653fed397c1
#fuzz[manual] Fuzz tests feed thousands of mutated and random files to the parser: each must parse and round-trip stably, or raise HcsSyntaxError.
  > test/fuzz.test.ts::assertWellBehaved #13847c57eb6e

## Providers
#providers[manual] Providers are openai (any compatible API), ollama, gemini, groq, openrouter and anthropic, called at temperature 0 with usage accounting; Bearer keys may be absent when a proxy injects them; 429/503 retries honor Retry-After and Google's retryDelay, and waits over 120 s, or a provider still failing after every retry, raise a quota error.
  > src/llm.ts::postJSON #f804a89279ad
  > src/llm.ts::retryDelayMs #53c59bd9ac2f
  > src/llm.ts::MAX_RETRY_WAIT_MS #ffea888e2d7e
#proxy[manual] Behind HTTPS_PROXY the CLI re-runs itself once with --use-env-proxy so that Node's fetch uses the proxy; auth errors say whether a proxy-injected key was rejected (x-proxy-error header) or no key was sent.
  > src/cli.ts::rerunBehindProxy #865c33840a44
  > src/llm.ts::authHint #ffdcc6547ae0
#rpm[manual] `--rpm` (or HCS_RPM) spaces requests evenly with one limiter per model spec; `--reasoning-effort` (or HCS_REASONING_EFFORT) is sent as `reasoning_effort` only when given.
  > src/llm.ts::RateLimiter #5c815985358a
  > src/llm.ts::createLLM #e1653e3a53e5

[probes]
?p1 How many hex characters of the SHA-256 digest does an anchor hash keep?
  = 12
  > src/anchors.ts::HASH_LENGTH #0330f2780307
?p2 What status does a symbol anchor get when the same symbol, unchanged, is found in another file?
  = moved
  > src/anchors.ts::checkSymbolAnchor #707de082a68e
?p3 Which format versions can this reader parse?
  = HCS/0.1, HCS/0.2 and HCS/0.3
  > src/format.ts::SUPPORTED_VERSIONS #bfa61b8b8d04
?p4 What happens to a compiled claim whose quote is not found in the source?
  = it is discarded
  > src/compile.ts::anchorFor #5e3194b4874f
?p5 How many points does a partial answer earn in the fidelity score?
  = 0.5
  > src/score.ts::POINTS #f5b535d01ef1
?p6 What is the longest server-requested wait HCS accepts before declaring the quota exhausted?
  = 120 seconds
  > src/llm.ts::MAX_RETRY_WAIT_MS #ffea888e2d7e
?p7 What is the largest source file size the compiler reads by default?
  = 256 KiB
  > src/sources.ts::collectSources #c0440aacf4c2
?p8 Which MCP tool returns the exact source text behind a claim id?
  = hcs_expand
  > src/mcp.ts::TOOLS #fdf64141fd1e
?p9 What tag do claims with high-risk injection patterns receive?
  = suspect
  > src/compile.ts::extractChunk #b8d51ae71481
?p10 How many bootstrap resamples does the confidence interval use by default?
  = 2000
  > src/score.ts::bootstrapCI #09a88d67acf9
